        "_note": "A magnetar is not a separate kind of object: it is a neutron star with a very strong field, so it is not SPAWNED. Generation draws star/NS and the field decides the label. The boundary is a PRODUCT CHOICE inside a real continuum - magnetars sit at 1e14-1e15 gauss and ordinary pulsars near 1e12, with high-B pulsars occupying the decade between - so it lives here as data rather than as a constant in code.",
