        "_subclass_note": "THE DIGIT IN G2V, ANCHORED RATHER THAN TABULATED. A subclass is a position in temperature inside its letter, and the real sequence is unevenly spaced - G0 to G2 is 160 K and K5 to K7 is 340 - so a linear split of the letter's band is wrong everywhere except by accident. These are effective temperatures for named MAIN-SEQUENCE subclasses (Pecaut & Mamajek 2013), and anything between them is interpolated. Sparse on purpose: only the well-measured anchors are stated, because inventing the gaps would be inventing data. NO PARAMETER BANDS BELONG HERE - since luminosity is computed and the classifier works from HR position, a subclass needs nothing but its temperature. A pack describing a different classification scheme replaces this block; a pack that omits it gets letters with no digit, which is a designation that states less rather than one that states something wrong.",
